<title>JAPAN: Japan jobless rate falls to 3.2 pct in March.</title>
<headline>Japan jobless rate falls to 3.2 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's seasonally adjusted unemployment rate in March fell to 3.2 percent, down from 3.3 percent in February and its lowest level in 12 months, the government said on Friday.</p>
<p>The jobs-to-applicants ratio was unchanged from the previous month at 0.73, the Labour Ministry said. This means there were 73 job openings for every 100 job seekers.</p>
<p>In fiscal 1996/97, ended March 31, the jobless rate rose to 3.3 percent from 3.2 percent the year before, but was below the 3.4 percent in calendar 1996.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the jobs data:</p>
<p> (Adjusted)			  March     February  Year ago</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		  3.2 pct   3.3 pct   3.2 pct</p>
<p>					 March     February  Year ago</p>
<p> Jobs-to-applicants ratio	 0.73	0.73	0.67</p>
<p> (Unadjusted)			March     February  Year ago</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		  3.5 pct   3.5 pct   3.5 pct</p>
<p> Number of unemployed	     2.34 mln  2.30 mln  2.29 mln</p>
<p> Number of employed		 March		year/year change</p>
<p> Overall				64.89 million	+1.4 pct</p>
<p>Main Industries:</p>
<p> Manufacturing			14.38 million	+0.8 pct</p>
<p> Services			     16.27 million	+4.2 pct</p>
<p> Wholesale, retail, restaurants 14.59 million	+0.1 pct</p>
<p> Construction			  6.89 million	+1.3 pct</p>
<p> Agriculture			   3.02 million	+4.5 pct</p>
</text>
